---

import { orgPaths } from '../../../lib/tenant-paths';
export const getStaticPaths = orgPaths;

import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../../components/PageHead.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Corrections and retractions"
  description="The three things that can happen to a published record when something is wrong, and who authorizes each."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Policies"
    title="Corrections and retractions"
    lede="A published record is never quietly edited. What separates a record from a blog post is what happens when something in it turns out to be wrong."
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <table class="tbl">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Mechanism</th>
          <th scope="col">When</th>
          <th scope="col">What the page shows</th>
          <th scope="col">Authorized by</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><b>Correction</b></td>
          <td>A factual error: a wrong number, a mislabeled figure, a misstated unit.</td>
          <td>A dated correction notice at the top. The text is amended and both facts are stated.</td>
          <td>An editor</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><b>New version</b></td>
          <td>A substantive revision: new data, expanded analysis, a changed conclusion.</td>
          <td>The new version at the same address, with earlier versions kept and linkable.</td>
          <td>An editor</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><b>Retraction</b></td>
          <td>Fabrication, plagiarism, an ethics failure, or a request from the authors.</td>
          <td>The page stays reachable, marked as retracted, with a dated notice and the reason.</td>
          <td>The faculty advisor, in writing</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:32px">
      <h2>Why a retracted record stays up</h2>
      <p>
        Because deleting it does not delete the copies people already have. Someone holding
        a downloaded version needs to be able to find out that it was withdrawn and why.
        Retracted records stay in search results here, clearly marked, for exactly that
        reason.
      </p>

      <h2>What does not need a notice</h2>
      <p>
        A typo that changes no meaning is fixed silently. Anything that changes what a
        reader would conclude gets a notice, and the test is the reader's conclusion, not
        the size of the edit.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting something wrong</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="/contact/">the contact address</a> with the record identifier and
        what you believe is incorrect. Reports from outside are treated the same as reports
        from authors.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
